1v3u|n|To clear (a liquid) from scum or substance floating or lying thereon, by means of a utensil that passes just beneath the surface; as, to skim milk; to skim broth. ; To take off by skimming; as, to skim cream. ; To pass near the surface of; to brush the surface of; to glide swiftly along the surface of. ; Fig.: To read or examine superficially and rapidly, in order to cull the principal facts or thoughts; as, to skim a book or a newspaper. ; To pass lightly; to glide along in an even, smooth course; to glide along near the surface. ; To hasten along with superficial attention. ; To put on the finishing coat of plaster.	a:97b,48,3;1nk7,25,3;15kq,1,1~1nk7,25,3;97b,48,3;15kq,1,1	v:uum,9,3;1s7f,5,1;17l2,2,6~17l2,2,6;uum,9,3;1s7f,5,1	V:1s7f,34,7~1s7f,34,7	n:27b2,41,2~27b2,41,2	N:19ln,63,2~19ln,63,2
